<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivation of Optimal Test Statistics</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we derive the analytical LLR for both tasks. Although the marginal problem involves latent task parameters <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, conditioning on the context <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> renders the hypotheses <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> simple for each episode. Classical Neyman-Pearson optimality therefore applies at the episode level, and the optimal decision statistic is given by the likelihood ratio conditioned on <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. The following derivations make this dependence explicit for the two task families considered.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Task A: Shifted Mean Discrimination</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\{\mu,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\{\mu,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The class-conditional distributions are isotropic Gaussians with means <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}=\mu+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}=\mu+k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}=-\mu+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}=-\mu+k</annotation></semantics></math>, and covariance <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=I</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{N}(m,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{N}(m,I)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p(x\mid m)=-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi)-\frac{1}{2}\|x-m\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(x\mid m)=-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi)-\frac{1}{2}\|x-m\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The LLR is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Lambda(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Lambda(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\|x-(\mu+k)\|^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\|x-(-\mu+k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\|x-(\mu+k)\|^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\|x-(-\mu+k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mu^{\top}x-2\mu^{\top}k." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mu^{\top}x-2\mu^{\top}k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the optimal statistic is affine in <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\top}(x-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\top}(x-k)</annotation></semantics></math>; correct classification requires centering with respect to the context-dependent shift.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Task B: Variance Discrimination</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For centered Gaussians with variances <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p(x\mid\sigma)=-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma^{2})-\frac{\|x\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(x\mid\sigma)=-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma^{2})-\frac{\|x\|^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The LLR is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Lambda(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Lambda(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{d}{2}\log\frac{\sigma_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}+\frac{\|x\|^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{0}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{d}{2}\log\frac{\sigma_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}+\frac{\|x\|^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{0}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The first term is a constant bias, while the data-dependent term is proportional to the energy <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the optimal statistic is purely quadratic.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Code, results, and figures are available on <a href="https://github.com/farischaudhry/implicit-likelihood-ratio-transformer" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">GitHub</a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Model Architecture</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a toy Transformer architecture designed for set-to-scalar tasks, which we refer to as <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformer</span>.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Type:</span> Bidirectional Transformer Encoder (PyTorch <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nn.TransformerEncoder</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layers:</span> 2</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention Heads:</span> 4</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Embedding Dimension (<math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{model}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{model}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> 128</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feedforward Dimension (<math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{ff}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{ff}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> 512</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Activation:</span> GELU</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalization:</span> Post-LayerNorm (<span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">norm_first=False</span>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input Processing:</span>
The input <math id="A2.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>16</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{16}</annotation></semantics></math> is linearly projected to <math id="A2.I1.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{model}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{model}</annotation></semantics></math>. The binary label <math id="A2.I1.i8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is projected via a separate learnable linear layer. These two projections are combined via element-wise addition to form the final context token embedding, effectively binding the label information to the input features via superposition.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Positional Encodings:</span> Standard learned absolute positional embeddings are added to the sequence.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Task Specifications</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Data is generated on-the-fly during training. Each batch consists of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=64</annotation></semantics></math> independent episodes.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task A: Shifted Mean (Linear).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input Dimension:</span> <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=16</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Context Size:</span> <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Latent Parameters:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I2.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discriminative direction <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\sim\text{Unif}(\mathbb{S}^{d_{x}-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\sim\text{Unif}(\mathbb{S}^{d_{x}-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Nuisance shift <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{k}^{2}I_{d_{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{k}^{2}I_{d_{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shift Magnitude:</span> <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}=3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}=3.0</annotation></semantics></math> (Training), <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}=9.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}=9.0</annotation></semantics></math> (Out-of-distribution (OOD) evaluation).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Generation:</span> <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mid y\sim\mathcal{N}(k+(2y-1)\mu,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mid y\sim\mathcal{N}(k+(2y-1)\mu,I)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task B: Variance (Nonlinear).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input Dimension:</span> <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=16</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Context Size:</span> <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Latent Parameters:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I3.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Class 0 Scale <math id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}\sim\text{Unif}[0.5,3.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}\sim\text{Unif}[0.5,3.0]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Class 1 Scale <math id="A2.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}\sim\text{Unif}[0.5,3.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}\sim\text{Unif}[0.5,3.0]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Generation:</span> <math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mid y\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{y}^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mid y\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{y}^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Training Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Models are trained to minimize the Binary Cross Entropy loss on the query label <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Optimizer:</span> AdamW (<math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9,\,\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9,\,\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-4</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scheduler:</span> OneCycleLR.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initial Learning Rate:</span> <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Batch Size:</span> 64 tasks per step.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Duration:</span> 20 epochs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Seeds:</span> Accuracy results are reported over 3 random seeds.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Ablation Variants</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the mechanism of in-context learning, we evaluated several model variants. Each variant tests a specific hypothesis regarding the inductive bias or information flow required for the task.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Positional Encodings (<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NoPos</span>, <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FrozenPos</span>).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard Transformers use positional encodings to process sequences. However, the statistical tasks (shifted mean, variance) are permutation invariant with respect to the context examples. Namely, the learned methodology should be permutation-invariant like sufficent statistics are.</p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerNoPos</span>:
We completely remove the learned positional embeddings (<math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=0</annotation></semantics></math>). This tests whether the model treats the context as a set rather than a sequence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerFrozenPos</span>: We initialize positional embeddings randomly but freeze them during training. This tests whether the model requires learned positional information or can utilize random absolute position markers.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Attention Mechanism (<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FrozenAttention</span>, <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FrozenQK</span>).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We test whether the attention heads must learn a task-specific metric space or if they can function as random associative memories.</p>
<ul id="A2.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerFrozenQK</span>: The Query (<math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>) and Key (<math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>) projections are frozen at initialization. Only the Value (<math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>) and Output (<math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{O}</annotation></semantics></math>) matrices are trainable. This enforces a fixed, random similarity kernel.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerFrozenAttention</span>: All attention weights (<math id="A2.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V},W_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V},W_{O}</annotation></semantics></math>) are frozen. Only the feedforward MLPs and embedding projections are trainable.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tokenization Strategy (<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Interleaved</span>).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our default architecture sums input and label embeddings: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}=\text{Proj}(x_{i})+\text{Proj}(y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Proj</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Proj</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}=\text{Proj}(x_{i})+\text{Proj}(y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, effectively binding the label to the input in a single token.</p>
<ul id="A2.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerInterleavedEmbeddings</span>: We replace the bound representation with a standard GPT-style interleaved sequence <math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x_{1},y_{1},x_{2},y_{2},\dots,x_{q}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x_{1},y_{1},x_{2},y_{2},\dots,x_{q}]</annotation></semantics></math>. This tests whether the additive binding is a necessary inductive bias for efficient learning at this scale (<math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=2</annotation></semantics></math> layers).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Label Dependence (<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NoLabels</span>, <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ShuffledLabels</span>).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These ablations verify that the model is performing supervised mapping (<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\to y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\to y</annotation></semantics></math>) rather than unsupervised clustering (<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\to x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\to x</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
<ul id="A2.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerNoLabels</span>: The context consists only of <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> vectors; <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> information is zeroed out.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerShuffledLabels</span>: The <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> labels in the context are randomly permuted within the batch, destroying the specific <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\to y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\to y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> mapping while preserving the marginal distribution of labels.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformerNoisyLabels</span>: During training, a fraction <math id="A2.I8.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of the context labels are flipped (<math id="A2.I8.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leftrightarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leftrightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>). This tests the model’s ability to aggregate evidence robustly despite contradictory data points.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Supplementary Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Task A OOD Generalization Analysis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess whether the model has learned the exact symbolic form of the likelihood ratio or a local approximation, we evaluate it on OOD task where the nuisance shift magnitude <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is increased from <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.0</annotation></semantics></math> (training) to <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.0</annotation></semantics></math> (validation).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ C.1 Task A OOD Generalization Analysis ‣ Appendix C Supplementary Experimental Results ‣ Implicit Statistical Inference in Transformers: Approximating Likelihood-Ratio Tests In-Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents the learning dynamics and final decision geometry for this OOD setting.</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization Gap (Left):</span> While the training accuracy converges rapidly to <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 78\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>78</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 78\%</annotation></semantics></math> (consistent with the in-distribution baseline), the OOD validation accuracy lags significantly, plateauing at <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 64\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 64\%</annotation></semantics></math>. The delayed rise in validation accuracy suggests a form of partial “grokking,” where the model gradually refines its decision rule, but the persistent gap indicates that the learned mechanism does not fully capture the invariant symbolic structure needed for perfect extrapolation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regression Degradation (Right):</span> The correlation between the model’s logits and the true LLR drops from <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\approx 0.86" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.86</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\approx 0.86</annotation></semantics></math> (in-distribution) to <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\approx 0.57" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.57</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\approx 0.57</annotation></semantics></math>. The increased scatter suggests that the model’s internal approximation of the sufficient statistic (<math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\top}(x-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\top}(x-k)</annotation></semantics></math>) is calibrated only for the training support and becomes brittle under large shifts.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Taken together, these results support the hypothesis that the Transformer implements an amortized approximate inference algorithm: it constructs a decision boundary that mimics the optimal LLR geometry locally, but relies on heuristics that degrade when the task parameters drift far from the training distribution.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10573v1/figures/appendix_fig1.png" id="A3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/204;" width="494" height="204" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span><span id="A3.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OOD Generalization Degradation (Task A).</span> <span id="A3.F3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Left)</span> Learning curves show a significant generalization gap: while the model masters the training distribution (blue), it struggles to extrapolate to large shifts (orange), achieving only partial generalization. <span id="A3.F3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Right)</span> The correlation with the true LLR degrades to <math id="A3.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.567" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.567</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.567</annotation></semantics></math>; the learned decision rule is a local approximation rather than the exact symbolic LLR.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Full Ablation Results</h3>

<figure id="A3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="A3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full Experimental Results.</span> We report mean accuracy <math id="A3.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 95% CI over 3 seeds for all experimental conditions. The oracle rows represent the theoretical upper bound (Bayes-Optimal Classifier) computed using the true latent task parameters. The model is close to the oracle on Task B, while Task A ablations demonstrate the necessity of learned attention mechanisms.</figcaption>
<div id="A3.T2.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:278pt;vertical-align:-136.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-0.6pt,0.4pt) scale(0.997235908013769,0.997235908013769) ;">
<table id="A3.T2.4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiment / Condition</span></th>
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Variant</span></th>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Train Acc (%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Val Acc (%)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="4"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theoretical Oracle</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Task A (Shifted Mean)</th>
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLR</span></th>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="84.6\pm 1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>84.6</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">84.6\pm 1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Task B (Variance)</th>
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLR</span></th>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="84.0\pm 1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>84.0</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">84.0\pm 1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="4"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Main Tasks</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Task A (Shifted Mean)</th>
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformer</span></th>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="77.5\pm 1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>77.5</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>1.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">77.5\pm 1.1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A3.T2.4.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="78.3\pm 0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>78.3</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">78.3\pm 0.3</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.4.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Task B (Variance)</th>
<th id="A3.T2.4.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A3.T2.4.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICLTransformer</span></th>
